  "scores": {
    "pmf": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "The fork count supported by c3 provides a limited developer-adoption signal consistent with the rubric, but contributor independence, active integrations, retention and paying usage remain unverified."
    },
    "narrative": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "c2 establishes a specific multi-currency settlement tool for AI agents, and the supported portion of c12 adds adjacent services and integrations; differentiation and a credible commercial path from tooling to platform remain unproven."
    },
    "execution": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "c8 and c9 establish meaningful aggregate shipping activity, while the supported portions of c4 and c5 show multiple contributors; c10 establishes the core repository's last push date, but sustained recent core-product delivery and rapid standards updates are not demonstrated."
    }
  },
  "recommendation": "watch",
  "missing_risks": [
    "Forks may reflect copying or experimentation rather than retained users; independent production deployments remain unknown.",
    "Commercial ownership, pricing, revenue capture and defensibility relative to the underlying protocol are unclear.",
    "Liquidity depth, executable spreads, settlement reliability and demand for non-dollar corridors are unverified.",
    "Signer controls and deployment safeguards lack independent security validation in the supplied evidence.",
    "Dependence on the underlying protocol, stablecoin issuers and operational counterparties could constrain reliability and distribution.",
    "Aggregate repository activity may obscure maintenance concentration or limited progress on the core product.",
    "The conflicting tool counts warrant checking documentation freshness and the actual shipped interface.",
    "Regulatory obligations and responsibility for failed or unauthorized settlements remain unclear."
  ],
  "strongest_counterargument": "The evidence establishes shipped tooling and a modest developer signal, but does not establish recurring customer demand, production settlement usage or a business that captures value. A founder call may be premature until independent deployment evidence shows that multi-currency agent settlement solves an urgent problem and supports a defensible commercial wedge."
}
